{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_vision_problem_statement", "label": "The problem: the network is the obstacle", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "lines 5-11", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A laptop behind NAT, a locked-down corporate environment, a CI runner, an air-gapped review box that can still reach a git remote. The usual answer is deploying a broker, tunnel or relay, and the deployment costs more than the problem."}, {"id": "docs_vision_shared_infrastructure_as_transport", "label": "Existing shared infrastructure becomes the transport", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "lines 9-11", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two machines almost always already share a git repository, synced folder, object store or wiki: infrastructure that exists, is already authenticated, and is already allowed through the firewall."}, {"id": "docs_vision_transport_is_detail", "label": "Transport is an implementation detail", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 15", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Applications talk only to their local runtime, so swapping GitHub for a shared folder is a config change. Nothing above the transport manager may name a transport, because if it could, transport independence would be a slogan rather than a property."}, {"id": "docs_vision_delivery_once", "label": "Delivery is implemented once", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Most wanted backends are object stores with no delivery semantics. Asking every adapter author to reinvent polling, acknowledgement, deduplication and redelivery would produce a dozen subtly different sets of delivery bugs in packages the project does not control, so a store adapter implements four methods and the runtime supplies the rest."}, {"id": "docs_vision_adr_0001", "label": "ADR 0001: store and native transports", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "lines 17, 49", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_vision_no_change_for_existing_apps", "label": "Existing applications should not have to change", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 19", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proxy mode exposes a server that has no idea dead-drop exists. The SDK is for applications that want more, not a tax on applications that want less."}, {"id": "docs_vision_say_what_is_true", "label": "Say what is true", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 21", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At-least-once delivery and best-effort per-recipient ordering are stated plainly in guarantees.md rather than buried, and the security model says what is not protected as clearly as what is."}, {"id": "docs_vision_current_capabilities", "label": "What exists today", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "lines 23-25", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four transports (filesystem, git, github, memory), encryption, chunking, compression, retries, circuit breaking, failover, deduplication, health-based routing, structured logs, Prometheus metrics, tracing, proxy mode, static exposures, and a plugin contract stable enough for third parties."}, {"id": "docs_vision_more_transports", "label": "Roadmap: more transports as separate packages", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "S3-compatible storage, OneDrive and SharePoint are the gaps. GitLab, Bitbucket and Azure DevOps already work through the git transport by remote url and earn dedicated packages only if their APIs offer something git does not."}, {"id": "docs_vision_github_token_path", "label": "Roadmap: a token path for GitHub", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Authentication is delegated entirely to gh today; a REST path behind the existing GhClient seam would remove that dependency where installing gh is the hard part."}, {"id": "docs_vision_streaming", "label": "Roadmap: streaming large payloads", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 33", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A response is buffered whole today and capped at 32 MiB."}, {"id": "docs_vision_plugin_ecosystem", "label": "Roadmap: a plugin ecosystem", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 35", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The measure of success is a transport written by someone who has never read this repository's internals, passing the conformance suite on the first try."}, {"id": "docs_vision_non_goal_broker", "label": "Non-goal: not a message broker", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 39", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A round trip over a git remote costs seconds, not milliseconds. If you have Kafka, use Kafka. This targets the case where standing up infrastructure is the expensive part, not throughput."}, {"id": "docs_vision_non_goal_policy_evasion", "label": "Non-goal: not a way around your security policy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 41", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Data moves only through channels you are already authorised to use; features whose main purpose would be evading controls are rejected."}, {"id": "docs_vision_non_goal_service_mesh", "label": "Non-goal: not a service mesh", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 43", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No competition with Kubernetes, no service discovery at scale, no sidecars."}, {"id": "docs_vision_non_goal_database", "label": "Non-goal: not a database", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 45", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The transport holds messages in flight, with retention and a reaper. It is not storage to query."}, {"id": "docs_vision_history_single_interface", "label": "History: the rejected send/receive/acknowledge interface", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 49", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An earlier sketch specified one send/receive/acknowledge transport interface; implementation showed it was the wrong shape for the target backends and it became the two-kind contract."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_vision_problem_statement", "target": "docs_vision_shared_infrastructure_as_transport", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "lines 7-11", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_vision_transport_is_detail", "target": "docs_vision_shared_infrastructure_as_transport", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "lines 11-15", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_vision_delivery_once", "target": "docs_vision_adr_0001", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 17", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_vision_history_single_interface", "target": "docs_vision_adr_0001", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 49", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_vision_delivery_once", "target": "docs_writing_a_transport_store_contract", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "vision.md line 17, writing-a-transport.md lines 42-57", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_vision_history_single_interface", "target": "docs_writing_a_transport_native_transport", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "vision.md line 49, writing-a-transport.md lines 123-127", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_vision_say_what_is_true", "target": "docs_security_model_metadata_leak", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 21", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_vision_say_what_is_true", "target": "docs_security_model_hostile_storage", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "line 21", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_vision_say_what_is_true", "target": "docs_testing_can_cannot_rule", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/vision.md", "source_location": "vision.md line 21, testing.md line 46", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "d